/* Overrun enabled: on an error such as ORE, re-arm reception so it does not stall.
   The occurrences are counted in midi_rx_err. ORE means one byte on the wire was missed,
   which makes it the primary health metric for sustained reception (reported by MSTAT). */
void HAL_UART_ErrorCallback(UART_HandleTypeDef *huart)
{
    if (huart->Instance == USART1) {
        midi_rx_err++;
        HAL_UART_Receive_IT(&huart1, (uint8_t *)&midi_rx_buf, 1);
    }
}

/* ===== Implementation summary =====
   Implemented:
     - Signal path (PA8/PA9), 3-step Bias (PA10/PA11), 3-state Input filter (PB12/PB13/PB14)
     - 3-state Response (PB4/PB15), read from PB0/PB1
     - Four LED indication sequences (Bias=orange / Response=cyan / Input=green / MIDI-Learn=white)
     - Footswitch, latch/momentary, DIP switches, MIDI-IN/Thru, MIDI-Learn, PowerGood ADC
     - MIDI Thru passes every byte straight through, including our own toggle CCs and incoming 0xFE.
       Store-and-forward was removed because it broke on interleaved input.
     - MIDI-OUT Active Sensing (0xFE) sent every 250ms
     - Toggle settings changeable over MIDI
         CC83=Input / CC84=Response / CC85=Bias; value split into four bands to select the state.
         Active channel: DIP-SW4 OFF = fixed CH12 / ON = the MIDI-Learn channel (same rule as on/off).
         Moving a physical toggle clears the override. Received CCs are serialized through a ring
         buffer (midi_evt_*) so bursts such as a preset recall are not dropped.
         The MRECV command injects MIDI-IN bytes for testing from the CLI.
   Not implemented:
     - Unsolicited MIDI-OUT transmission other than Active Sensing (trigger conditions undecided)
   Hardware notes:
     - PB15 is the Response Gradual output.
       The NJW4191 OSC pin is tied to GND, the correct configuration when no external clock is used.
     - PC14 also drives D115 through the 74HCT04 (4A->4Y), so D114 and D115 blink in opposite phase.
*/

/* USER CODE END 4 */

